<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tewodros II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1818–<a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tewodros II was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1855 until his death in 1868. Rising from a provincial background, he ended the era of regional fragmentation known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zemene-mesafint">Zemene Mesafint</a> and sought to centralise and modernise the state. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> credit his reunification, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>'s centralisation, with rebuilding the administrative structure that later enabled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Adwa</a> campaign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tewodros-ii.jpg" alt="Tewodros II" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uncredited; derivative work by Vob08 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:T%C3%A9wodros_II_-_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
